# Checkout must not rewrite the bytes the export pinned.
#
# The mirror verifies itself with SHA-256 over the working tree, and a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` turns every LF into CRLF - so a clone of a
# correct tree failed verification, and `git checkout -- .` was enough to make a
# correct file fail. `eol=lf` keeps the shipped bytes on every platform; the rules
# below stay more specific and win where binary or precision content is involved.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and precision assets must not be re-encoded on checkout.
# Line-ending conversion changes the bytes of the tokenizer file, which is
# pinned by SHA-256 in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
*.onnx binary
*.wasm binary
*.txt -text
